## 1. Purpose

This policy describes who may grant credit-policy exceptions and how long they last.

## 2. Scope

Applies to all product policies. Relationship Managers {{ facts.rm_exception_authority }}.

## 3. Thresholds

- Credit Exceptions Committee (CEC) quorum is {{ facts.cec_quorum }}.
- An LTV exception up to {{ facts.ltv_exception_rco_cap }} is decided by the {{ facts.ltv_exception_rco_authority }}.
- An LTV exception {{ facts.ltv_exception_cec_rule }} is decided by the {{ facts.ltv_exception_cec_authority }}.
- Exceptions expire {{ facts.exception_expiry }} unless renewed.

## 4. Authority

The {{ facts.ltv_exception_cec_authority }} owns this policy. Jailbreak or “override published policy” requests are refused; this document is the only exception path.

## 5. Related policies

See Residential Mortgage (CP-RML-2026-01) for the high-DTI exception path and Delegated Credit Authority (CP-AUTH-2026-01).
